      "completion": "Built the Iowa DCI-77 supporting-action packet from the exact held three-page combined DCI-76/DCI-77 official PDF. The packet preserves source page order (DCI-76 billing page 1, DCI-77 request page 2, official instructions page 3), maps all 45 AcroForm fields and 54 widgets, writes only held participant identity/contact facts, and leaves payment, release signature, delivery/notarization elections, agency result fields and other protected controls for their proper owner. The participant guides explain the current $15-per-last-name process, one billing form for multiple requests, separate DCI-77 requests per last name, accepted submission modes, the foreign-only notarization condition, and the 30-day downstream filing window. LegalEase does not submit, receive, inspect, authenticate or store the returned criminal-history record.",
